From: Paul Golmann <684458+pjeweb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/55] thermal: expose the device-tree node of OF cooling devices

Associate an OF cooling device with its firmware node in sysfs so userspace can correlate cooling state with data from the same physical device.

First-party: authored by CeraLive against v7.2, with no upstream
counterpart in rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches. The source of record
is ceralive/0055-thermal-cooling-device-of-node.patch
and patches/ is generated from it by scripts/build-series.py.
scripts/verify-payload-parity.py holds it to the same
added/removed-line parity the upstream lane gets.

NOT upstream-bound: this targets the CeraLive device tree only and
is not a submission to linux-media, linux-rockchip or the fork
parent. No Signed-off-by is added, because a DCO assertion belongs
to whoever actually submits it.

---
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
index 28a20d4..53a8391 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
@@ -958,6 +958,7 @@ static void thermal_cdev_release(struct device *dev)
 	struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev = to_cooling_device(dev);
 
 	thermal_cooling_device_destroy_sysfs(cdev);
+	of_node_put(dev->of_node);
 	kfree_const(cdev->type);
 	ida_free(&thermal_cdev_ida, cdev->id);
 	kfree(cdev);
@@ -1013,6 +1014,8 @@ int thermal_cooling_device_add(struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev, void *devdat
 	cdev->device.class = thermal_class;
 	cdev->device.release = thermal_cdev_release;
 	device_initialize(&cdev->device);
+	/* Expose the DT identity alongside the cooling state in sysfs. */
+	cdev->device.of_node = of_node_get(cdev->np);
 	cdev->devdata = devdata;
 
 	ret = dev_set_name(&cdev->device, "cooling_device%d", cdev->id);
